<title>FRANCE: Bic shares hit new high after Tipp-Ex buy.</title>
<headline>Bic shares hit new high after Tipp-Ex buy.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in French pen and lighter manufacturer Bic rose as much as 4.71 percent to a record 890 francs after the company said it bought Tipp-Ex Holding GmbH which owns the German company that makes Tipp-Ex liquid eraser.</p>
<p>The terms of of the acquisition were not disclosed.</p>
<p>By 1255 GMT, Bic shares had slipped back to 881 francs, up 3.76 percent from Wednesday's close of 850 francs.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
</text>
